    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103355" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρᾰδ-ισταί</span></b> , οἱ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>young people who met to
				make merry on the fourth of the month</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				258
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>men born to a life of toil</i>, like Heracles, who
			was born <i>on the fourth of the month</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2a
				</span></i>
			, q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				309
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				754.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
